# Local Rails connectivity is selected by runtime capability, not credentials.
#
# scripts/dev-start --rails joins the explicitly configured private Podman
# network and exports EDGE_LOCAL_RAILS_ENABLED; the workspace's own `dev` script
# sets EDGE_LOCAL_NODE_RUNTIME=1. src/lib/rails-client.ts takes the direct
# transport only when it sees BOTH, and falls back to the VPC binding otherwise.
#
# This file carries no variables, and it cannot: `vite dev` runs the Worker in
# workerd, whose `process.env` is built from the Worker's own vars rather than
# from a .env file or from the shell. vite.config.ts is what bridges the two
# EDGE_LOCAL_* names across, and it does so only while SERVING — forwarding them
# during a build would bake them into the production artefact. Export them in the
# shell (or let compose.yaml do it); do not put them here.
#
# Cloudflare Access service-token credentials are consumed only by
# scripts/check-tunnel and never by the application runtime.
